IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`

-- Regulation 2 (interpretation), the definitions about people: blind, close relative, foster parent, health care professional,
-- looked after by a local authority, paid work, partner, prisoner, step-parent, terminally ill.
-- Each definition takes its facts as a record, so that a seat layer can build the record from plain answers.
-- Wherever a definition rests on another Act (a certificate, a section, a regulation), whether that holds is a stated input,
-- because those Acts are not among the inputs.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- blind
-- src:26 | “blind” means certified as severely sight impaired or blind by a consultant ophthalmologist;
@ref reg 2 "blind" (src:26)
DECLARE `Sight certificate` HAS
    `certified as severely sight impaired or blind`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:26 | “blind” means certified as severely sight impaired or blind by a consultant ophthalmologist;
@ref reg 2 "blind" (src:26)
GIVEN certificate IS A `Sight certificate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — blind` certificate MEANS
    (certificate's `certified as severely sight impaired or blind`) AND (certificate's `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- close relative, "in relation to a person". Limb (a) lists eleven relations; limb (b) adds the other member of a couple
-- of which one member is on the list. `relation of the partner to the person` is the relation the other member of the couple
-- has to the person; it is `not a listed relation` when the relative has no partner or the partner is not on the list.
-- src:34 | “close relative”, in relation to a person, means—
-- src:35 | (a) a parent, parent-in-law, son, son-in-law, daughter, daughter-in-law, step-parent, step-son, step-daughter, brother or sister; and
-- src:36 | (b) if any of the above is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple;
@ref reg 2 "close relative" (src:34-36)
DECLARE `Listed relation` IS ONE OF
    `a parent`
    `a parent-in-law`
    `a son`
    `a son-in-law`
    `a daughter`
    `a daughter-in-law`
    `a step-parent`
    `a step-son`
    `a step-daughter`
    `a brother`
    `a sister`
    `not a listed relation`

DECLARE `Possible close relative` HAS
    `relation to the person`                    IS A `Listed relation`
    `relation of the partner to the person`     IS A `Listed relation`

-- src:34 | “close relative”, in relation to a person, means—
-- src:35 | (a) a parent, parent-in-law, son, son-in-law, daughter, daughter-in-law, step-parent, step-son, step-daughter, brother or sister; and
-- src:36 | (b) if any of the above is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple;
@ref reg 2 "close relative" (src:34-36)
GIVEN relative IS A `Possible close relative`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — close relative` relative MEANS
    (NOT (relative's `relation to the person` EQUALS `not a listed relation`))
    OR (NOT (relative's `relation of the partner to the person` EQUALS `not a listed relation`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- foster parent. England and Wales: a person with whom a child is placed under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review
-- Regulations (England 2010; Wales 2015). Scotland: a foster carer or kinship carer with whom a child is placed under the
-- Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009. Whether the placement is under those Regulations is a stated input.
-- src:48 | “foster parent” means—
-- src:49 | (a) in relation to England, a person with whom a child is placed under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (England) Regulations 2010;
-- src:50 | (b) in relation to Wales, a person with whom a child is placed under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (Wales) Regulations 2015;
-- src:51 | (c) in relation to Scotland, a foster carer or kinship carer with whom a child is placed under the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009 ;
@ref reg 2 "foster parent" (src:48-51)
DECLARE `Placement of a child with a person` HAS
    `nation in which the child is placed`                                 IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer`                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:48 | “foster parent” means—
-- src:49 | (a) in relation to England, a person with whom a child is placed under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (England) Regulations 2010;
-- src:50 | (b) in relation to Wales, a person with whom a child is placed under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (Wales) Regulations 2015;
-- src:51 | (c) in relation to Scotland, a foster carer or kinship carer with whom a child is placed under the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009 ;
@ref reg 2 "foster parent" (src:48-51)
GIVEN placement IS A `Placement of a child with a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — foster parent` placement MEANS
    CONSIDER placement's `nation in which the child is placed`
    WHEN England  THEN placement's `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations`
    WHEN Wales    THEN placement's `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations`
    WHEN Scotland THEN (placement's `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations`) AND (placement's `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- health care professional (except in regulation 98, where regulation 98(4) gives its own meaning; uc4 encodes that one).
-- src:53 | “health care professional” means (except in regulation 98)—
-- src:54 | (a) a registered medical practitioner;
-- src:55 | (b) a registered nurse; or
-- src:56 | (c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999 ;
@ref reg 2 "health care professional" (src:53-56)
DECLARE Practitioner HAS
    `registered medical practitioner`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered nurse`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `occupational therapist or physiotherapist`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:53 | “health care professional” means (except in regulation 98)—
-- src:54 | (a) a registered medical practitioner;
-- src:55 | (b) a registered nurse; or
-- src:56 | (c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999 ;
@ref reg 2 "health care professional" (src:53-56)
GIVEN practitioner IS A Practitioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — health care professional` practitioner MEANS
    (practitioner's `registered medical practitioner`)
    OR (practitioner's `registered nurse`)
    OR ((practitioner's `occupational therapist or physiotherapist`) AND (practitioner's `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- looked after by a local authority, "in relation to a child or young person": looked after within the meaning of any of
-- three statutes. Whether the child is so looked after under each is a stated input.
-- src:74 | “looked after by a local authority” in relation to a child or young person means a child or young person who is looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989 , section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014;
@ref reg 2 "looked after by a local authority" (src:74)
DECLARE `Care of a child` HAS
    `looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:74 | “looked after by a local authority” in relation to a child or young person means a child or young person who is looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989 , section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014;
@ref reg 2 "looked after by a local authority" (src:74)
GIVEN care IS A `Care of a child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — looked after by a local authority` care MEANS
    (care's `looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989`)
    OR (care's `looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995`)
    OR (care's `looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- paid work: work done for payment or in expectation of payment, but not being engaged by a charitable or voluntary
-- organisation, or as a volunteer, where the payment received or due is in respect of expenses.
-- src:82 | “paid work” means work done for payment or in expectation of payment and does not include being engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer, in circumstances in which the payment received by or due to be paid to the person is in respect of expenses;
@ref reg 2 "paid work" (src:82)
DECLARE `Work done by a person` HAS
    `work is done for payment or in expectation of payment`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `person is engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment received or due to be paid is only in respect of expenses`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:82 | “paid work” means work done for payment or in expectation of payment and does not include being engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer, in circumstances in which the payment received by or due to be paid to the person is in respect of expenses;
@ref reg 2 "paid work" (src:82)
GIVEN work IS A `Work done by a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — paid work` work MEANS
    (work's `work is done for payment or in expectation of payment`)
    AND (NOT ((work's `person is engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer`) AND (work's `payment received or due to be paid is only in respect of expenses`)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- partner: the other member of a couple (except in regulation 77, which uc2 encodes). Whether a person is a member of a
-- couple is the Act's section 39 (a stated input); the claim basis (regulation 3) records it.
-- src:83 | “partner” means (except in regulation 77) the other member of a couple;
@ref reg 2 "partner" (src:83)
GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — the claimant has a partner` basis MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `a single claimant`                              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `joint claimants`                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a single claimant who is a member of a couple`  THEN TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- prisoner: detained in custody pending trial or sentence, or under a sentence, or on temporary release under the Prison Act
-- 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989; but not a person detained in hospital under the mental health Acts.
-- src:87 | “prisoner” means—
-- src:88 | (a) a person who is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court; or
-- src:89 | (b) is on temporary release in accordance with the provisions of the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989 ,
-- src:90 | other than a person who is detained in hospital under the provisions of the Mental Health Act 1983 or, in Scotland, under the provisions of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 or the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 ;
@ref reg 2 "prisoner" (src:87-90)
DECLARE Detention HAS
    `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts`                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:87 | “prisoner” means—
-- src:88 | (a) a person who is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court; or
-- src:89 | (b) is on temporary release in accordance with the provisions of the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989 ,
@ref reg 2 "prisoner" limbs (a) and (b) (src:87-89)
GIVEN detention IS A Detention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — prisoner, limbs (a) and (b)` detention MEANS
    (detention's `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction`)
    OR (detention's `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court`)
    OR (detention's `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989`)

-- src:87 | “prisoner” means—
-- src:88 | (a) a person who is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court; or
-- src:89 | (b) is on temporary release in accordance with the provisions of the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989 ,
-- src:90 | other than a person who is detained in hospital under the provisions of the Mental Health Act 1983 or, in Scotland, under the provisions of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 or the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 ;
@ref reg 2 "prisoner" (src:87-90)
GIVEN detention IS A Detention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — prisoner` detention MEANS
    (`reg 2 — prisoner, limbs (a) and (b)` detention)
    AND (NOT (detention's `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- step-parent, "in relation to a child or qualifying young person (A)": not A's parent, and either (a) a member of a couple
-- whose other member is a parent of A, both being responsible for A; or (b) previously such a member, responsible for A
-- immediately before the couple ended and ever since. "Responsible for" is regulation 4 (uc1), taken here as a fact.
-- src:104 | “step-parent”, in relation to a child or qualifying young person (“A”), means a person who is not A’s parent but—
-- src:105 | (a) is a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of A, where both are responsible for A; or
-- src:106 | (b) was previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of A, where immediately prior to ceasing to be a member of that couple the person was, and has since continued to be, responsible for A.
@ref reg 2 "step-parent" (src:104-106)
DECLARE `Relationship to a child or qualifying young person` HAS
    `person is a parent of A`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `person is a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of A`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person and that parent are both responsible for A`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `person was previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of A`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before ceasing to be a member of that couple the person was responsible for A`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `since then the person has continued to be responsible for A`                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:105 | (a) is a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of A, where both are responsible for A; or
@ref reg 2 "step-parent" limb (a) (src:105)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship to a child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — step-parent, limb (a)` relationship MEANS
    (relationship's `person is a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of A`)
    AND (relationship's `the person and that parent are both responsible for A`)

-- src:106 | (b) was previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of A, where immediately prior to ceasing to be a member of that couple the person was, and has since continued to be, responsible for A.
@ref reg 2 "step-parent" limb (b) (src:106)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship to a child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — step-parent, limb (b)` relationship MEANS
    (relationship's `person was previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of A`)
    AND (relationship's `immediately before ceasing to be a member of that couple the person was responsible for A`)
    AND (relationship's `since then the person has continued to be responsible for A`)

-- src:104 | “step-parent”, in relation to a child or qualifying young person (“A”), means a person who is not A’s parent but—
-- src:105 | (a) is a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of A, where both are responsible for A; or
-- src:106 | (b) was previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of A, where immediately prior to ceasing to be a member of that couple the person was, and has since continued to be, responsible for A.
@ref reg 2 "step-parent" (src:104-106)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship to a child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — step-parent` relationship MEANS
    (NOT (relationship's `person is a parent of A`))
    AND ((`reg 2 — step-parent, limb (a)` relationship) OR (`reg 2 — step-parent, limb (b)` relationship))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- terminally ill: suffering from a progressive disease where death in consequence of it can reasonably be expected within
-- 12 months. The number of months is a fact only a clinician can give; when there is no progressive disease it is never read.
-- src:108 | “terminally ill” means suffering from a progressive disease where death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 12 months;
@ref reg 2 "terminally ill" (src:108)
DECLARE Illness HAS
    `suffering from a progressive disease`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected`        IS A NUMBER

-- src:108 | “terminally ill” means suffering from a progressive disease where death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 12 months;
@ref reg 2 "terminally ill" (src:108)
`reg 2 — the months within which death must be expected for a person to be terminally ill` MEANS 12

-- src:108 | “terminally ill” means suffering from a progressive disease where death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 12 months;
@ref reg 2 "terminally ill" (src:108)
GIVEN illness IS AN Illness
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — terminally ill` illness MEANS
    (illness's `suffering from a progressive disease`)
    AND ((illness's `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected`) AT MOST `reg 2 — the months within which death must be expected for a person to be terminally ill`)
